DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       iiddllee()  is an internal system call used during bootstrap.  It marks the
       process’s pages as swappable, lowers its priority, and enters the  main
       scheduling loop.  iiddllee() never returns.

       Only  process 0 may call iiddllee().  Any user process, even a process with
       superuser permission, will receive EEPPEERRMM.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       iiddllee() never returns for process 0, and always returns -1  for  a  user
       process.

EERRRROORRSS
       EEPPEERRMM  Always, for a user process.

